From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:37:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] let a teleport wait for the entity's handover to finish

D-40: a plugin that teleports the same entity twice in one tick gets true
then false, and the second teleport silently does not happen. Paper does
both.

Measured, not argued: a cross-region teleport does not move the entity, it
builds a copy (transformForAsyncTeleport) and hands it to the destination
region, which adds it to its lookup on a later tick. In that window the copy
is in no level's lookup, so canTeleportAsync() refuses through
hasNullCallback(). Nothing sets the callback to NULL - the copy is born with
it from the field initialiser, and the destination's add is the first thing
ever to set it.

CraftEntity#teleportAsync already has a path for "not ours to move right
now": schedule on the entity's own EntityScheduler. The handover window was
not taking it, because isOwnedByCurrentRegion is still true - the entity has
not moved, only changed hands. Widen the condition.

No ownership check is bypassed, no owner is guessed, nothing is dispatched to
the global region scheduler, no callback or validity is faked, and the
calling thread does not wait. Inline, this window can only produce false, so
this widens and never narrows.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java
index b10a72af64aff0bb3683854ab6fb841874f786c4..fbdd2b02c9298c21c598d04531a577b8c0b1ec4d 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java
@@ -1198,7 +1198,12 @@ public abstract class CraftEntity implements org.bukkit.entity.Entity {
                 ret.complete(Boolean.FALSE);
             }
         };
-        if (org.bukkit.Bukkit.isOwnedByCurrentRegion(this)) {
+        // Lecithin start - D-40: a previous teleport may still be handing this entity over. It is
+        // still owned by this region (it has not moved, only changed hands), so the inline path
+        // below would claim it and the platform would refuse it for having no level callback yet.
+        // Take the scheduler path the platform already has for "not ours to move right now".
+        if (org.bukkit.Bukkit.isOwnedByCurrentRegion(this) && !fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinTeleportHandover.isMidHandover(this)) {
+        // Lecithin end
             run.accept(this.getHandle());
             return ret;
         }
